  "result": "Perfect! All 83 tests pass \u2713. I've successfully added line discount support:\n\n**src/errors.js:**\n- Added `DISCOUNT_INVALID` error code\n\n**src/invoices.js:**\n- Added `isValidDiscountPercent()` helper to validate discounts (0-100, can have decimals)\n- Updated `createInvoice()` to accept and validate `discountPercent` on each line\n- Added `lineDiscount(line)` \u2014 calculates discount for a line (line total \u00d7 discountPercent / 100), using `roundCents()` and clamping to 0\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, total }` where:\n  - `discount` is the sum of all line discounts\n  - `total = subtotal - discount` (never negative)\n- Updated `addLine()` to accept and validate `discountPercent`, replacing it when adding to existing SKUs\n\n**src/render.js:**\n- Updated to show discounts on line items: `(12.5% off: -\u20ac59.38)`\n- Shows expanded total line when discounts present: `Subtotal: ... Discount: ... Total: ...`\n- Keeps simple `Total: ...` format when no discounts\n\n**Tests (83/83 passing):**\n- 14 new tests in invoices.test.js covering: discount acceptance, validation, calculation, zero values, and negative clamping\n- 3 existing tests updated to expect `discount` field in `invoiceTotals`\n- 5 new tests in render.test.js covering discount rendering in various scenarios",
